# Snapshot fixtures: preserve the bytes exactly as generated.
#
# These files are compared byte-for-byte against source-generator output, so they must not go
# through the repository's `* text=auto` line-ending normalization: it stores them with LF, and a
# checkout then materializes LF on Unix while the generators that produced them emit CRLF (a
# generator shipped as a NuGet package bakes the newlines of its own sources at package build time,
# so its output is CRLF on every host). Normalized fixtures therefore only ever matched on the
# platform whose checkout happened to restore the original endings.
* -text
